  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=-\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(-\\frac{2}{7})=106.601\\,549{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248{106.602}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${106.602}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={106.602}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={73.398}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={73.398}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13989949/assets/e378560486eca17f870b21743718c9f984f2bd3bf5609601f1cea674e15018e6.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{73.398}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={253.398}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=106.602\\cdot 253.398\u224827\\,013,\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
